From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: resolution list of fractions of the native pixels as a
 render scale, gamma slider as interface scale

What common/0008 does for Android, on iOS. SDL lists the screen in points, once per orientation; the settings window offers 100% down to 25% of its pixels instead, applied at once. The window keeps filling the screen in points: a resolution is the scale SDL's view is rendered at (Alpha3::setRenderResolution in the support library), [Video] resolution is applied that way at startup too. As on Android, a smaller resolution makes the interface larger on the screen, and the gamma slider sets its scale ([GUI] scaling factor).
Mouse positions are scaled from points to pixels by a fraction instead of a whole number, and a Metal window (ANGLE) reports its pixels through SDL_Metal_GetDrawableSize (SDLUtil::getDrawableSize).
